cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Patchwork: A CWE-Labelled Corpus of Real Patched Vulnerabilities"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - alias: TayR-D
repository-code: "https://github.com/TayR-D/patchwork-cve"
url: "https://github.com/TayR-D/patchwork-cve"
abstract: >-
  16,597 real, already-patched public CVEs, each paired with its fix commit and a
  structured analysis of the vulnerability: CWE classification, root cause, taint
  source and sink, why the patch works, and a proposed detection heuristic. Labels
  are produced by two independent model passes and scored against the MITRE CWE
  hierarchy; disagreements are resolved by a third adjudication pass that sees both
  analyses anonymised and order-randomised. Disagreement is preserved on every row.
  Ships with a leakage-verified, group-aware train/eval split for vulnerability
  detection and CWE classification research.
keywords:
  - vulnerability detection
  - security dataset
  - CVE
  - CWE
  - static analysis
  - software security
  - machine learning
  - patch analysis
  - taint analysis
  - application security
  - security research
  - benchmark
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-03"
